WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:07.966
Can she see me yet?

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:08.967
I can!

00:00:09.217 --> 00:00:11.553
This is pretty cool technology
you got here.

00:00:11.928 --> 00:00:13.263
So, let me try that. 

00:00:15.306 --> 00:00:16.891
We’re playing footsies! 

00:00:17.308 --> 00:00:18.852
We should have done this in 
outer space!

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:22.147
We could have both been 
sitting on, like, Neptune,

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.982
in a bubble.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.901
Hey, what have you been
doing for fun?

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.321
I have not left home since 
March 8.

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:31.239
At all?

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.199
I went to an eye doctor’s 
appointment

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.786
because I could no longer fix
my eye infection

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:39.622
on telemedicine.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:43.043
And then I went for 
a mammogram. 

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:46.504
I asked what did you 
do for fun.

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:50.425
Eye doctors and mammograms
do not qualify.

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:52.635
I have never had a mammogram, 
myself

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:53.762
Okay, so for fun.

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:55.013
but it doesn’t sound fun. 

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.849
You can do better than that.

00:00:57.974 --> 00:01:00.310
No, it is, definitely, not.
Here’s what I did for fun:

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.479
I’ve had two girls here, 
the whole time,

00:01:03.104 --> 00:01:04.689
who were living in Los Angeles, 

00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:06.441
who moved here during 
the pandemic

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.942
They’ve been fun.

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:10.653
We have movie nights, just the
two girls, Stedman, and I.

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:12.822
We do regular movie nights,

00:01:12.989 --> 00:01:15.408
and I’ve seen all the movies I 
wished I’d seen and didn’t.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.787
We watched every episode 
of “The Crown.”

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:23.041
We started a whole thing with 
Popsicles, so we now have—

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.709
That sounds fun.

00:01:24.876 --> 00:01:27.253
—twenty-three different
flavors of Popsicles,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.380
including pumpkin, 
and sweet potato.

00:01:29.547 --> 00:01:32.383
And we have Friday-night
dance nights

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.302
We put puzzles together.

00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:37.305
And I’ve read a lot. 
What have you done?

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.224
You know, we went—

00:01:39.974 --> 00:01:42.393
—for example—Michelle and
I went bike riding yesterday,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.104
which was fantastic,

00:01:44.562 --> 00:01:46.147
because it was a beautiful day.

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:49.109
And game nights

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:52.946
—big!—although sometimes,
I get too competitive.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.615
At least, that’s what 
Michelle says,

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.826
because she’s been losing.

00:02:01.371 --> 00:02:03.706
Hello, President Barack Obama!

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:05.458
Hey you! How are you?

00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:08.711
I’m so good! 
You’re in Washington, DC,

00:02:08.837 --> 00:02:10.547
and I’m home, in Santa Barbara,

00:02:10.672 --> 00:02:12.507
but—through the miracle 
of technology

00:02:12.674 --> 00:02:14.801
—we get to be face to face in
the same room,

00:02:15.009 --> 00:02:17.053
and we don’t even have 
to wear masks! 

00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:18.805
And we have a fire going, 
apparently!

00:02:19.055 --> 00:02:20.723
And we have a fire going

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.350
—a real one, too!

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:25.979
I’m excited to talk to you 
about your extraordinary

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:27.856
—I mean, I don’t even have 
words for it,

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:31.317
—it’s a masterful rendering of
your presidency and life,

00:02:31.442 --> 00:02:32.986
“A Promised Land.”

00:02:33.403 --> 00:02:35.280
But first, I just want to 
ask you,

00:02:35.446 --> 00:02:37.532
What was the one word that would

00:02:37.615 --> 00:02:39.242
best describe how you felt
when it was

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.744
announced that Joe Biden 
and Kamala Harris will be

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.705
the next President and
Vice President

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:45.248
of the United States?

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:46.499
I was thrilled! 

00:02:46.624 --> 00:02:48.334
"Joe Biden"!

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.253
First of all, obviously, Joe

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:52.422
is somebody who

00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:53.590
stood by me

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.551
on every major decision I 
had for eight years. 

00:02:56.718 --> 00:02:59.387
He's become a brother 
-a genuinely good friend.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.972
Kamala was one of my

00:03:01.097 --> 00:03:04.350
earliest supporters when I 
first launched my presidency

00:03:04.642 --> 00:03:06.895
So, I’m personally invested
in them.

00:03:07.478 --> 00:03:10.231
And they have the character 
and experience, I think,

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.484
to do an outstanding job

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:17.488
in a very difficult time,

00:03:17.614 --> 00:03:19.616
a very challenging time, in 
this country.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:23.912
But, beyond the personal 
investment I have in them,

00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:27.749
I think this gives us a
chance to

00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:33.463
get back to the kind 
of competent,

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:38.301
caring government that we 
so badly need,

00:03:38.635 --> 00:03:46.059
and that the world expects out
of the United States of America.

00:03:46.351 --> 00:03:49.020
So, it’s not going to 
immediately solve every

00:03:49.187 --> 00:03:51.439
every problem that we have

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:55.235
—because you have enormous
challenges, around COVID

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.279
and the economic after effects;

00:03:58.529 --> 00:04:01.282
you’ve got long-standing issues,

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:04.619
like racial bias in the 
criminal justice system,

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:08.164
and rising inequality

00:04:09.374 --> 00:04:12.001
—but without this change, I think,

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:15.630
things would have continued
to deteriorate,

00:04:15.964 --> 00:04:20.635
and our democracy would have
been much more fragile.

00:04:20.802 --> 00:04:22.762
And I’m confident

00:04:23.012 --> 00:04:24.847
a new President 
and Vice President

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.307
are gonna help us 
right the ship.

